---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Print a request as code for another language or tool

Usage: rustman export snippet [OPTIONS] [REQUEST]

Arguments:
  [REQUEST]
          The request: a request file, its id (path without .rman.yaml) or its name

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          The language (see --list); `fetch`, `python` and `rust` are aliases

      --list
          List the supported languages and exit

      --show-secrets
          Print secret values instead of «redacted:<name>» placeholders

      --placeholders
          Keep variables unresolved: {{name}} in shell tools, constants in code

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
